  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 157 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nWinds will increase again on Friday ahead of a low pressure\nsystem making its way across the Central Plains. The associated\ncold front will bring rain showers across the state,\nparticularly Saturday afternoon and into the overnight hours.\nWith a few hundred joules/kg of CAPE, a few rumbles of thunder\nwithin the showers is possible, but no severe weather is\nexpected. Total rainfall will likely total around a quarter \ninch for most areas.\n\n\nWarm temperatures Friday and Saturday in the 60s will cool after\nthe low pressure passes and high temperatures will only climb\ninto the upper 30s and 40s, closer to normal, for Sunday into\nnext week.",
